Kellen Winslow: Kellen Boswell Winslow Sr. (born November 5, 1957) is a former American football player in the National Football League (NFL).  A member of the Pro Football Hall of Fame (1995), he is widely recognized as one of the greatest tight ends in the league's history.  Winslow played his entire NFL career from 1979 to 1987 with the San Diego Chargers after being selected in the first round of the 1979 NFL Draft.  He played college football for the University of Missouri, where he was a consensus All-American.  He was also inducted into the College Football Hall of Fame (2002).

